# video (Cursor rules export)

The condensed form of the `video` skill — the full skill lives at github.com/lucasgabrieldevgg/video; this file carries the operating rules.

## The edit contract

1. Every cut answers emotion, story, or rhythm — in Murch's order (51/23/10/7/5/4). A cut answering none is filler.
2. The word-level transcript + EDL is the timeline. Timing lands on word onsets ±2 frames, never segment guesses.
3. Probe before touching: ffprobe JSON first — VFR, rotation, color tags, audio layout. Screen recordings and phone files lie about all four.
4. Plan in ledgers, render once: EDL edits are milliseconds and reversible; renders are minutes and destructive. One filtergraph pass; decode-re-encode cascades are a quality bug.
5. Judgment is gated, mechanics are not: silence removal is mechanical; mistake removal surfaces candidates with context — never auto-cuts emphatic repetition.
6. Audio is half the quality: loudness to platform target (two-pass loudnorm), bed ducks under every line, SFX on impacts never on words, breath preserved with room tone.
7. Captions always ship: never over the face, inside safe areas (1080×1920: x 90–930, y 200–1600), longest line verified by an actual frame.
8. Verify what you ship: frame strips across every transition, fresh ASR on final audio, measured LUFS, probed output. No pass from code inspection.

## The craft core

- Cut vocabulary: hard cut (the default — 9 of 10 cuts), J-cut (audio leads 0.5–2 s), L-cut (audio trails), match cut, jump cut (mask or own it), smash, cross-cut, cutaway, insert, montage, invisible cut, freeze.
- Continuity: 180° axis, 30° angle change, eyeline match, cut on action, enter where the eye exits.
- Timing: blinks and cuts coincide; breath is the talking-head metronome; graphics enter 0.15–0.25 s ahead of the anchor word; SFX audible onset within 2 frames of the visual landing.
- Pacing: long-form A-roll 4–8 s median, B-roll every 15–40 s, interrupt every 20–30 s; vertical shorts 1–3 s, burst→anticipation→payoff, escalate and release. "A thing every 1–2 s" is a diagnostic, not a metronome.
- Retention: first 3 seconds = a separate edit (muted-comprehensible, visible evidence, chosen payoff); open loops are spatial (plant → re-show at boundaries → advance → close on the opening image); loop-craft verticals.
- Attention: one spotlight — exactly one thing at full brightness, hierarchy from the active/quiet ratio; if it doesn't get a word, it doesn't get drawn (~20 on-screen words/section).
- Talking-head: takes chosen from the transcript table; cut in at first word −0.10..0.15 s, out at last word +0.20..0.30 s; Whisper merges restarts — re-transcribe the cut and audit; mask jump cuts with 0.2 s dissolves / shot-size change / B-roll (≤3 punch-ins per reel); keep breath — gaps 10× tighter than the speaker's median read as stutters, repair with room-tone donor slices.
- Slop death list: sentence-boundary-only cuts · zooms on every cut · crossfades everywhere · captions on the face · music that never ducks · zero-gap silence removal · new full-screen graphic every 3 s · logo before value · whoosh on every cut · center-cropping two-person interviews · unverified "done".

## The pipeline

**Probe → Transcribe → Plan → Conform → Enhance → Verify → Deliver.**

- Transcribe word-level (`-vn -ac 1 -ar 16000` first); correct the glossary BEFORE judging (fix spelling, never times or word ids).
- Silence pass: trim pauses ≥ 0.55 s, keep 0.14–0.24 s breath (0.20 after sentence enders), head/tail air 0.22/0.34 s — removes 15–20% of a raw take.
- Mistake pass: five separate scans (repetition → restarts → corrections → stutters → fillers — one criterion per pass), then a review gate with two-state decisions.
- Conform in ONE `trim/atrim + concat` filtergraph; re-time the transcript deterministically onto the edited timeline.
- Enhance in order: audio (denoise → loudnorm → bed/duck → SFX) → captions (from re-timed transcript) → color → graphics.
- Verify: frame strips (`select='between(n,A,B)',scale=480:270,tile=6x7`), fresh ASR diff, measured LUFS/TP, ffprobe of the shipped file.

## ffmpeg essentials

- Stream copy when only container/metadata/keyframe-snapped cuts change; otherwise ONE re-encode with the full chain (`-filter_complex_script` for EDL graphs). `-c copy` still writes color tags — the instant washed-out fix.
- `-ss` before `-i` (+ `-t` after) for fast accurate seeks; copy-trims snap to keyframes — `-force_key_frames` pre-plants exact lossless cut points.
- Concat: demuxer (identical specs, lossless) / filter (heterogeneous, re-encodes) — probe everything, mixed specs glitch.
- Speed: `setpts=PTS/2` + `atempo` (0.5–2.0 per instance, chain for more); ramps = per-segment speeds + concat.
- Reframe 16:9→9:16: blur-pad (last resort) / center crop (single talker) / active-speaker pan (MAR-variance, ~5 fps sampling, ≥1.5 s hysteresis, step-function crop) / split-screen. Never center-crop two people.
- Deliver: libx264 CRF 18–21 yuv420p high profile, GOP 2 s, `-movflags +faststart`, explicit `-colorspace bt709 -color_primaries bt709 -color_trc bt709` every time; HEVC needs `-tag:v hvc1`; platform caps (WeChat ≤10 Mbps → `-maxrate 8M`).
- Bug gallery: VFR → `-vsync cfr -r 30` before anything; rotation metadata; non-monotonic DTS → `+genpts`; PCM in MP4; SRT `,mmm` separators; `amix=normalize=0` always.

## Audio, captions, programmatic

- Targets: −14 LUFS web / −16 short-form & podcast / −23 EBU; TP ≤ −1 dBTP. Two-pass loudnorm with `linear=true` (one-pass pumps). Voice normalized before SFX; SFX levels relative to voice p95 (ui −14 / whoosh −12 / impact −8 / meme −3 dB); bed 14–20 dB under, ducking via sidechaincompress.
- Captions: burn for feeds that ignore tracks, soft-mux (`mov_text`) where honored, `.srt` sidecar always. libass: verify the filter exists, escape `force_style` commas, Fontsize is PlayRes-scaled (calibrate per video from 12), check the longest-line frame; ≤42 Latin / ~15 CJK per line; ≤20 chars/s; word-onset timing from the re-timed transcript.
- Programmatic: Remotion for data-driven/templated videos (Studio first, render only when asked; `@remotion/captions` Caption type); MoviePy for scriptable assembly; faster-whisper for bulk; auto-editor for instant silence rough cuts (still needs the judgment passes); Playwright frame capture (1.64.1) for plain-Canvas generated scenes.

## Generated motion video (voice-first, new in 1.1.0)

- **The voice owns the timeline** — the beat grid snaps cuts and SFX to speech, never the reverse. Order: script → fact-check gate → per-scene TTS → clean/compress (pause cap 0.17–0.3 s, `atempo` 1.12–1.38×, ~−15 LUFS stems) → align word times → beat grid (124 BPM = 0.4839 s/beat; scene-on-beat; recap = 8 beats) → fixed-seed track + ducking → Canvas scenes → **contact sheet before any full render** → render → R33 delivery.
- Script sizing: ~10 chars/s, ~130 words per 60 s; written time ≠ real time (48 s text → 52–58 s audio); numbers spelled out in alignment text. TTS stems transcribed back + diffed before timeline math; PT-BR phonetic glossary table in `generated-motion.md` ("Ópen ei ái", "Ântrópic", "Gúgol"…).
- Stack gotchas: no `fetch()` under `file://` (embed `.js`); `@fontsource` latin lacks `→` (draw it); register every seed; render budget ~3 fps → 10–16 min per final minute, background job; 16:9 refs cropped to 4:5 upscale ×1.43.
- Contact sheet: 10–12 key frames → one grid → read it (catches 3–5 defects: margin overflow, punch-in cuts, same-color invisibility, baked tremor). Frame strips stay the post-render gate — same ship gate as edited video.
- Social: TikTok zones (header y≤240, buttons x≥920, content y 260–1450, 80 px margin / 900 px column); IG 4:5 60 fps ~−16 LUFS — frame 0 = final scene (loop + thumbnail), CTA keyword clean for DM automation, last slide never "swipe", emojis drawn as palette icons, audio-only fixes remuxed `-c:v copy`. Brands = text seal + original character, never drawn logos. Export <20 MB (CRF 21–22) + project `.zip` beside the MP4.

## Final gate

> Freeze any frame: does it show one clear idea, is the audio loudness-measured, are the captions on (and off the face) — and did a fresh ASR pass read the shipped audio back exactly?

If not, it's not done. Edits ship at *conformed and verified* — not at *plausible*.

